{"type":"result","key":"v2:b12ea19cbee3d04c6259c10507c7ae4466e917707d5a856efe10455eac373c02","agentId":"a05ac85ee61485e57","result":{"slug":"chain-addsink-ordering","committed":true,"files":["src/QueryPipeline/Chain.cpp"],"summary":"Fixed `Chain::addSink` in /workspace/src/QueryPipeline/Chain.cpp, which inserted the new processor with `processors.emplace_front(...)` (copy-paste from `addSource`) after connecting it to the current output port. This put the sink at the head of the processor list, corrupting the chain's input/output port accessors (`getInputPort`/`getSource` then returned the sink). Changed it to `processors.emplace_back(...)` so the sink lands at the tail, matching the documented `source -> transform -> ... -> sink` ordering."}}
